{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human","id":1324121,"title":"To be a hero, or to be human?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-12T20:24:09-07:00","id":1324121,"title":"To be a hero, or to be human?","content":"Or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> Hey folks, I\u2019m currently facing an in-character conflict, literally in-character as my Zenith is struggling within herself. She identifies as \u2018a simple country monk\u2019 (insert your own southern accent and braces-snapping, they\u2019re accurate for her) but her NPC WiFi, Abyssal girlfriend and unintended cult of mortal followers all believe she\u2019s amazing and aren\u2019t afraid to tell her.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s not one to hide her abilities (She\u2019s maxed-out on STR, has good mental stats and multiple 5-dot craft masteries) but she really does view herself as just a normal person who can do things others can\u2019t. She\u2019s struggling with accepting herself as anything special...but she\u2019s a Solar.<br /> <br /> I guess the real question is, when does your character outgrow their pre-exaltation sense of self and embrace their new role?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:51:23-07:00","id":1324129,"title":"","content":"I tend to play characters that are on board with being heroes...from the moment they exalt, if not before. I've had a few players play characters not entirely sure of themselves or their own power, but only rarely (and they all play nights...), but most characters I've ST'd for think their something special (if not going full hubris).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T23:55:16-07:00","id":1324160,"title":"","content":"Harry Potter never thinks of himself as special, even when training armies and using artifacts crafted by death himself to defeat the world's most powerful wizard. And he has people saying he's special from day one.<br /> <br /> Save it for Limit Break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T01:10:14-07:00","id":1324163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324129#post1324129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a few players play characters not entirely sure of themselves or their own power, but only rarely (and they all play nights...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, curious. The only player character I haver ever seen in my group that wasn\u00b4t sure of his status as a Solar was a Night Caste (with strong Immaculate beliefs: when he was a mortal he worked as a scout for a Shikari). Maybe that\u00b4s a Night Caste thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T01:27:01-07:00","id":1324166,"title":"","content":"Hah my forst exalted character ever was a Twilight that had an irrational fear of zombies, all the way until I retired him as an Essence 7 complete badass. Not like a paralyzing fear they just still gave him the wibblies. <br /> <br /> More to the point, as a monk I think your character\u2019s position has a great opportunity to evolve into a kind of wisdom. Maybe she never really sees herself as special or above anyone else, just that she has different challenges set before her to overcome. The real question is, is changing her self perspective something you want to do? Or feel is necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T02:54:30-07:00","id":1324173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human#post1324121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when does your character outgrow their pre-exaltation sense of self and embrace their new role?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should one?<br /> <br /> Certainly, they're all going to keep being human in any case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T03:44:35-07:00","id":1324176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human#post1324121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folks, I\u2019m currently facing an in-character conflict, literally in-character as my Zenith is struggling within herself. She identifies as \u2018a simple country monk\u2019 (insert your own southern accent and braces-snapping, they\u2019re accurate for her) but her NPC WiFi, Abyssal girlfriend and unintended cult of mortal followers all believe she\u2019s amazing and aren\u2019t afraid to tell her.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s not one to hide her abilities (She\u2019s maxed-out on STR, has good mental stats and multiple 5-dot craft masteries) but she really does view herself as just a normal person who can do things others can\u2019t. She\u2019s struggling with accepting herself as anything special...but she\u2019s a Solar.<br /> <br /> I guess the real question is, when does your character outgrow their pre-exaltation sense of self and embrace their new role?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pffft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Your WiFi: the greatest teacher of martial arts!<br /> <br /> It feels almost bad to give advice to someone at the same metaphorical table as me but FWIW: taking on a higher level of responsibility and power does not make you inhuman. It just means you're a human with power. You have to think about your actions, what you're able to accomplish for better or worse. An Exalt can do things a Humble Monk can not. They've the insight and wisdom to lead a monastic movement, write scriptures and create doctrine. You've the power to act on the macro level, it's just all within you rather than being the result of your position in the world.<br /> <br /> Now, you don't have to do that. An Exalt can show restraint, whatever retcon BS 3E added in about 'Essence Fever'. *does disco move*. But not acting like that is a choice too. You're either accepting the current state of the world, or denying that you are worthy of shaping it. Your actions will probably still be significant but only in either in maintaining the status quo, or in changes wrought incidentally in the pursuit of smaller goals. You beat up the bad guy who was threatening you, fine, but now their city's unstable, stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T06:24:39-07:00","id":1324198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324176#post1324176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Exalt can show restraint, whatever retcon BS 3E added in about 'Essence Fever'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your view of Essence Fever is mistaken if you think it constrains character behaviour like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T08:59:47-07:00","id":1324215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324198#post1324198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your view of Essence Fever is mistaken if you think it constrains character behaviour like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know it doesn't constrain, but it's presented as normal: the default way a young Chosen will normally act. Even without it, similar pressure on Exalts to 'act epic' has always been there. But it's a new thing from Ex3, I don't care for it for a few reasons, so one more for the complaints pile!. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T09:41:59-07:00","id":1324218,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that you've actually got two, rather separate questions here. The first is &quot;When should my character stop thinking of themselves as 'normal' and accept that they're exceptional&quot;, and the second is &quot;when do I stop being human?&quot;. And I would argue that the answer to the second, at least, can very well be &quot;never&quot;. Because the Exalted <i>are</i> human. I think that's a pretty fundamental part of the game's themes - the Exalted have been given great power, sure, but they're still <i>humans, </i>with human drives and motivations, human triumphs, and human flaws. If they stopped being human when they exalted, they'd be less subject to human morality, and questions at the heart of Exalted, like &quot;what would you do if you were given the power to accomplish your goals?&quot;, stop being as meaningful.<br /> <br /> And of all the Exalted, I'd argue that the Solars in particular are the <i>most</i> human. Their powers are basically human abilities, simply pumped to the maximum. Sure, the Unconquered Sun's Essence gives them a fiery, sunlight-feeling <i>theme</i>, but the basic nature of what He gives is excellence. When a Solar swordswoman uses Peony Blossom Attack to make two deadly strikes in less than a heartbeat, when a Solar preacher unleashes Terrifying Apparition of Glory and strikes awe into the hearts of all who look upon her, or a Solar crafter uses her bare hands to beat a bar of iron on the forge because Craftsman Needs No Tools, those are all things that are what someone who's <i>extremely</i> good at Melee, Presence, or Craft can just <i>do</i> in Creation. They're not external &quot;spells&quot; or powers granted by Sol Invictus, he's just supplying the power of excellence needed to raise those skills to that kind of incredible pitch (in fact, my headcanon is that sometimes very skilled mortals, in times of extreme stress and focus, can pull off what are effectively Solar charms. It's just, without the Exaltation backing it up, those heights of skill aren't easily repeatable. And, often, it's a moot point, because achieving that sort of effect on your own is practically <i>begging</i> for a Solar Exaltation to notice you anyway, so they become capable of doing it again anyway). <br /> <br /> The upshot of the Solars being the most &quot;human&quot; of the Exalted, though, is that it's actually a worse thing for them to lose that sense of connection and empathy with mortals than any other type of Exalt. If a Lunar, for example, comes to the conclusion that she's basically a monster, a quicksilver shapeshifter with no true face, only what she presents to the world, well, that's <i>true</i>. It doesn't mean she has to stop caring for humans. But a Solar who comes to the conclusion that &quot;Hey, I've got all this power, I'm basically a god, not a human at all&quot; has lost sight of a key truth of her nature, that she <i>is</i> human, and the things she accomplishes are something any human could do, if they tried hard enough. That means she's either lost her empathy, or, even worse, deliberately cut herself off from it, and is probably well on the road to becoming the sort of tyrant who justifies the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the question of whether your character is human aside, let's address the other question, of when it's appropriate for her to stop believing she's just &quot;normal&quot;, and &quot;nothing special&quot;. I'd say there's two main ways of approaching this, the characterization one, and the dramatic one. What I mean by that is that the characterization approach considers what the most believable way for your character to come to the conclusion would be, based on her personality, influences, etc., while the dramatic approach considers when it would be most appropriate to make the decision based on narrative considerations, when it would be most dramatic to happen.<br /> <br /> For the characterization approach, you've got to decide exactly how strong the character's belief in her normality is. I assume it's an Intimacy, because if it's just an idle belief without much emotional stock in it, the character comes off more as just foolish for believing something that's clearly not true. Now, game-mechanically, even a Defining Intimacy could technically be eroded in as little as three scenes, assuming the ST agrees it hasn't been coming up. It could be removed even faster than that, if a strong social character put a lot of effort into eroding it and had some other Intimacies to oppose it. So, one way to both strengthen the characterization and mechanically boost you against attempts to remove the Intimacy when you don't want to is to make sure your other Intimacies support it. For a Principle of &quot;I'm just a normal woman, nothing special&quot;, other Principles like &quot;I hate people who set themselves up as better than others&quot; or Ties to people or things she knew before she Exalted are good. These can be used to get resolve bonuses against attempts to change the core Intimacy, and to do decision points if the attempts do succeed. Conversely, the supporting Intimacies can be a useful guide to how long it takes to change the central one - if you have to abandon or change the context on all of them before tweaking that central Intimacy, it puts a useful brake on how fast you shift. Personally, I'd go with having three or four supporting Intimacies, and limiting myself to reducing or changing the context to one per session. Assuming the central Intimacy was at the Defining level, that would mean it would be between 5 sessions (assuming all the supporting ones were only at Minor level) and 12 sessions (assuming the supporters were all Defining as well) before I could completely remove the central Intimacy of &quot;I'm just this guy, you know?&quot;<br /> <br /> Narratively, on the other hand, while still a question of Intimacies, depends much less on other supporting Intimacies (though I still recommend having some, to provide support against having the central one removed before you're ready). Instead, you want to look for dramatic moments to declare the Intimacy has changed. There's really too many potential dramatic moments to ever list them all, of course, but here's a couple classics:<ul><li>A contrasting character: a character appears who's fully embraced the idea that being a Exalt makes them better and not human. To make this work, they do have to be legitimately impressive, not just a poser or otherwise empty. The dramatic moment can come when your character beats them in some kind of conflict, thus proving her superiority, but giving her a chance to say &quot;Yes, I am special, but that doesn't mean I'm not human! I'm not like you, I can accept I'm skilled without giving up my humanity.&quot;</li> <li>A dark reflection: This is almost the opposite of the above suggestion, a character who's <i>too much</i> like yours. They've got a similar belief in their own &quot;normalcy&quot;, and it's harming themselves and those around them - perhaps they're refusing to use their abilities, or rejecting the responsibility people are trying to give them, leaving others without guidance. The dramatic opportunity here is for your character to step up and say &quot;I realize I'm not normal, but that means I have to use my powers as best I can, to help people.&quot; If you can drop the line &quot;With great power comes great responsibility&quot;, bonus points.</li> <li>Some great catastrophe or event is happening, and only your character is capable of solving it. To really set up the drama, several other people that your character previously considered &quot;above&quot; them (parents or other family members, civil authorities, religious figures, etc.) should try and fail, before your character finally has to step up and do her job. In the aftermath, she can accept that she's not &quot;normal&quot;, but that means she can help more people. Again, &quot;With great power comes great responsibility&quot; is a good line at this point.</li> </ul>Notably, the narrative route requires more cooperation from the ST, because they've got to introduce NPCs and situations to give you those opportunities. You should be talking to them regardless of your approach, so that you're on the same page, but it's particularly important to do so when you're trying to be dramatic about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T12:27:34-07:00","id":1324245,"title":"","content":"For a monk character, a constant tension between humility and the breadth of capability seems quite fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324215#post1324215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the default way a young Chosen will normally act. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's an emotional impulse described as taking as little as a few months to bring under control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324218#post1324218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Lunar, for example, comes to the conclusion that she's basically a monster, a quicksilver shapeshifter with no true face, only what she presents to the world, well, that's <i>true</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the way that the line between humanity and monstrosity is presented as something that presents no inherent conflict or challenge for Lunars, I realised something about the majority of their Charms when thinking about what worked so well in the absence of making them Animal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Namely that those powers also have an essential humanity which defines their overall character. The guiding themes are just different than Solars.<br /> <br /> I mean, no real inner self and just a face presented for society's sake? What, is that something that no human has ever struggled with?<br /> <br /> You know what's really inhuman? Inhospitality being punished with lightning bolts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T14:46:52-07:00","id":1324276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324215#post1324215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even without it, similar pressure on Exalts to 'act epic' has always been there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still prefer Essence fever to 2e's &quot;epic Motivations.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324215#post1324215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's a new thing from Ex3...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it was introduced by <b>1e</b>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T15:58:18-07:00","id":1324290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324245#post1324245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an emotional impulse described as taking as little as a few months to bring under control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which leaves it still in play for most starting parties? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> dang... Really? That's hilarious! One more stupid thing from 1e instead. (because players really need an excuse to... do things ^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T16:05:36-07:00","id":1324293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324290#post1324290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more stupid thing from 1e instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not you like it, I'd appreciate it if you stopped calling it stupid, as it's something that I and a few of my friends enjoy about the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324290#post1324290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(because players really need an excuse to... do things ^^)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sometimes they do. Considering that there are people in Creation intent on hunting the PCs down and killing them, some players tend to focus on laying low and staying hidden; it helps to have a reminder that the game is still ultimately about being Big Damn Heroes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T17:03:33-07:00","id":1324307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324276#post1324276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still prefer Essence fever to 2e's &quot;epic Motivations.&quot;<br /> <br /> Actually, it was introduced by <b>1e</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually actually, 1e introduced it due to its not being edited out (much like Chosen of Saturn having been Orangesids in the early iterations) and made no mention of it beyond the paragraph where it appeared for the rest of the edition. 3e dusted the concept off and changed a few bits, namely Essence Fever being a temporary thing that's like growing pains for the Chosen, as opposed to a presumable freak-out mechanic replaced by Limit Break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T17:14:04-07:00","id":1324309,"title":"","content":"&quot;I guess the real question is, when does your character outgrow their pre-exaltation sense of self and embrace their new role?&quot;<br /> <br /> When they realize somebody else might get it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T17:30:07-07:00","id":1324312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324307#post1324307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually actually, 1e introduced it due to its not being edited out...</div> </div> </div> </div>Introduced is introduced. Moreover, Holden said otherwise; I'm having trouble finding the post, but he actually discussed at one point how he himself assumed it was an editing error, until he talked to Grabowski during the development of Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-13-2019, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T19:07:34-07:00","id":1324329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324290#post1324290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which leaves it still in play for most starting parties? </div> </div> </div> </div>The default starting character has been Exalted for around a year. The general assumption seems to be that the heady rush of magic puberty has faded into background noise.<br /> <br /> I find the point of Essence Fever to be conveying a sense of the profound qualia of becoming Exalted. That the transformation is not a neutral, unnoticed thing, even if it doesn't take long to settle down, although thereafter it can be a powerful surge of adrenaline under the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> I'm sure we've all had powerful emotional moments driven by a special kind of achievement or exertion, in which feelings are running high, sensations sharpen and judgement is a bit clouded, by which to sympathise. That doesn't mean we never settle down back into our hang-ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T23:11:36-07:00","id":1324365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324293#post1324293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not you like it, I'd appreciate it if you stopped calling it stupid, as it's something that I and a few of my friends enjoy about the game.<br /> <br /> Yes, sometimes they do. Considering that there are people in Creation intent on hunting the PCs down and killing them, some players tend to focus on laying low and staying hidden; it helps to have a reminder that the game is still ultimately about being Big Damn Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Really. We're supposed to be polite about things we dislike about the game now?<br /> <br /> 'cause if that's the case, I'd like a refund on people's insults around the Compass books, resonance, Magitech, the 2e Deathlord writeups, Virtues, the Thousand Dooms, the Thousand Stream River and basically every other aspect of 2e that wasn't actively offensive but was disliked by those who preferred 1e's tone. :P Oh yeah, and Motivations. Which you used snark quotes on in your very first post on this topic. Or the smug-bold of 'actually, it's from 1e', as if that somehow obviated my ability to complain about it?<br /> <br /> I mean... it's not like I insulted you, or your friends. I insulted an aspect of the game you like, that I don't care for. Is that seriously verboten around here?<br /> <br /> And that approach to Essence Fever contradicts how it's actually written up: as both temporary and very optional. If it's supposed to be an 'actually fight the Wyld Hunt' beatstick it's a singularly bad one. Motivation accomplished that far better for me: it compelled Exalts to act and offered mechanical bonuses for doing so, whilst providing flexibility. It's imperfect but it worked, and I feel its loss in 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324329#post1324329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default starting character has been Exalted for around a year. The general assumption seems to be that the heady rush of magic puberty has faded into background noise.<br /> <br /> I find the point of Essence Fever to be conveying a sense of the profound qualia of becoming Exalted. That the transformation is not a neutral, unnoticed thing, even if it doesn't take long to settle down, although thereafter it can be a powerful surge of adrenaline under the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> I'm sure we've all had powerful emotional moments driven by a special kind of achievement or exertion, in which feelings are running high, sensations sharpen and judgement is a bit clouded, by which to sympathise. That doesn't mean we never settle down back into our hang-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* in that case, I kinda find it going from redundant to pointless. When given the overwhelming power of Exaltation, who wouldn't test it? Push it? Someone could theoretically play the Shinji and try to avoid their ordained role, but that doesn't really fit metatextually with what a player is going to want out of their character. Ronnie Soak is a wonderful memorable figure but who wants to play as him prior to the events of Thief of Time?<br /> <br /> Hmm. I suppose the latter point ultimately nails my dislike of Essence Fever. I always loved the idea of Exaltation as lateral, a realignment of the soul, this great transcendental moment. 'Suddenly, everything stopped'. Emotions around the moment run strong, but the act of Exaltation is greater than that, at least as I play it, and the emotions brought to it are your own. All it does is act as a mirror for them. Essence Fever plays into Exaltation as less enlightenment and more soul battery, at least to me. 'You've an excess of energy that's pushing you to use it' vs 'You're at one with yourself and a power that's a part of you know'. Does that make sense? We're very resolutely in personal preference and reading territory here though.<br /> <br /> Trying to shift this back onto topic, this is an issue I feel Sticks faces. With an 'overwhelming energy' take on Exaltation, there's no real reason to change your perspective long term. You're basically a superhero. Essence Fever might encourage you to go out and punch a few villains, but that's about it. Motivation was there to try and get Exalted thinking bigger, enacting long term changes in the world. The choice here could be looked at as a choice between Essence Fever and it's more immediate scope, and a wider scale Motivation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The 3e/2e divide, brought down to an IC moment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T23:34:12-07:00","id":1324367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324365#post1324365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'cause if that's the case, I'd like a refund on people's insults\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>How much are you paying for people\u2019s insults?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324365#post1324365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, and Motivations. Which you used snark quotes on in your very first post on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t <i>like</i> it, but I didn\u2019t call it <i>stupid</i>. <br /> <br /> (And to be fair, I <i>have</i> called various things \u201cstupid\u201d in the past. Age-XP rules, giving Superman a gun, Janeway euthanizing an officer on <i>Voyager</i>, J.K. Rowling insisting wizards shit themselves, et cetera. But if someone in a discussion asks me to cut back on the hostility I generally apologize and try and do it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324365#post1324365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the smug-bold of 'actually, it's from 1e', as if that somehow obviated my ability to complain about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to not like something, but when I see a mistake, I often try and point it out. No smugness intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-14-2019, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T01:17:16-07:00","id":1324379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324365#post1324365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda find it going from redundant to pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also find it a bit pointless and irrelevant, but because it's pointless and irrelevant, it's easy to ignore, so it doesn't bother me. I suspect half my players don't even know it's a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Motivation was there to try and get Exalted thinking bigger, enacting long term changes in the world. The choice here could be looked at as a choice between Essence Fever and it's more immediate scope, and a wider scale Motivation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The 3e/2e divide, brought down to an IC moment! </div> </div> </div>You still have to have a Defining Intimacy, and you still have to have a Principle and Ties, so I think there's plenty of stuff to motivate PCs to do stuff (even if it's like Odysseus, where it's just about protecting your family).<br /> Tbh, my character's Defining Intimacy of &quot;The High Priest Not To Be Described must be defeated&quot; is basically a Motivation.<br /> <br /> Certainly I've never seen a low-XP 3e character not really want to do anything. Some high-xp characters, but that's due to character development. And isn't different to 2e: I completed my Lunar's Motivation in 2e, so had no Motivation for a while.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T01:21:54-07:00","id":1324380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human#post1324121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When does your character outgrow their pre-exaltation sense of self and embrace their new role?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the question is... do they have a new role? Because it's quite likely that what they wanted to do when they were a mortal is also what they want to do now; the difference is just that they have the power.<br /> <br /> If it's not (maybe they're pulled by responsibility, or other Exalts try and convince them to do it), well, that's the plot of many ancient myths and modern Superhero films. When does Spiderman realise he can't just have a normal high school life and has to be a hero? It's never something he gets entirely comfortable with, that's a tension running all the way through. Odysseus never accepts his role; he's just forced to abandon his family and fight a stupid war, and then pisses off the gods and is cursed to take a decade to return home. But he never actually wants to be an epic hero.<br /> And then there's plenty of heroes who get into it pretty quickly; but even they occasionally have the tension.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Our PCs still go to the pub/teahouse, try and get married, fall in love with the wrong people, and also are Essence 5 Solars and Lunars.<br /> <br /> Actually, the 300xp Night Caste who grew up on the streets and now is the brother-in-law of the Pharoah still hasn't really accepted his role of Prince; it involves things he finds traumatic (like beating his other brother-in-law to death because he was trying to overthrow the Pharoah with an army of the dead), so he's currently pretending to be an ordinary human martial artist and staying far away from the palace.<br /> <br /> It all depends on the character and circumstance, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-14-2019, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T01:32:17-07:00","id":1324383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324379#post1324379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still have to have a Defining Intimacy, and you still have to have a Principle and Ties, so I think there's plenty of stuff to motivate PCs to do stuff (even if it's like Odysseus, where it's just about protecting your family).<br /> Tbh, my character's Defining Intimacy of &quot;The High Priest Not To Be Described must be defeated&quot; is basically a Motivation.<br /> <br /> Certainly I've never seen a low-XP 3e character not really want to do anything. Some high-xp characters, but that's due to character development. And isn't different to 2e: I completed my Lunar's Motivation in 2e, so had no Motivation for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* Defining intimacies help, but their flexibility is a double edged sword. Not having a firm capital m Motivation allows for a wider variety of characters, but those new characters have less of an impulse to do what I view as Exalted type stuff. A Defining Tie or Principle at least gives the GM a good firm hook to get you into the action, but Motivations encouraged player proactivity. There was A Thing you wanted to do. (technically players tended to form passive motivations anyway, but the default was an active goal.)<br /> <br /> My own main current Ex3 character kinda fell into this trap, and (confession, we're players in the same game) I feel Sticks' did too. We both do things because we're engaged with the active story of the Chronicle, but neither of our PCs has any real firm end goal <i>outside </i>the confines of The Plot. Hence pondering what it means to be an Exalt, what other stuff they should be doing, and me framing it through the lense of motivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T04:40:48-07:00","id":1324414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324365#post1324365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the emotions brought to it are your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that the Exaltation is part of you, but it makes a contribution to your systems that is not?<br /> <br /> The emotions brought on by orgasm only happen because of the triggering of an endorphin rush arising from stimulation of the genitals, do they not belong to you either?<br /> <br /> Or is the issue that there's a separation between the Exaltation and the homunculus inside of a person's head?<br /> <br /> Are Inspire actions also objectionable for creating emotions from the external side of the dichotomy between false outer influences and genuine inner influences?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to shift this back onto topic, this is an issue I feel Sticks faces. With an 'overwhelming energy' take on Exaltation, there's no real reason to change your perspective long term. You're basically a superhero. Essence Fever might encourage you to go out and punch a few villains, but that's about it. Motivation was there to try and get Exalted thinking bigger, enacting long term changes in the world. The choice here could be looked at as a choice between Essence Fever and it's more immediate scope, and a wider scale Motivation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The 3e/2e divide, brought down to an IC moment!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. We've got so many interesting characters and scenarios because that notion that they've got to have an enormous scope of perspective in the long term has been dropped.<br /> <br /> The feeling that you can take over the world is an endorphin rush that will inevitably crash into the size and complexity of the world.<br /> <br /> Mind, maintaining humility does not need to make one incapable of being an influencer. Burned out inhabitants of the Age of Sorrows can be greatly compelled and inspired by such Integrity.<br /> <br /> I think one could plausibly make a game in which an Integrity focused Zenith who continues to view themselves as a humble monk is continuously challenged by beings looking to tempt them, or political figures trying to convince them towards grandeur, power and direct authority or continuously resisted by somebody trying to maintain perspective, humility and simple good works. People witness that, hear of it, and find hope in the idea, wanting to follow the example set.<br /> <br /> It's one way for the world to become better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T06:55:27-07:00","id":1324445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324414#post1324414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that the Exaltation is part of you, but it makes a contribution to your systems that is not?<br /> <br /> The emotions brought on by orgasm only happen because of the triggering of an endorphin rush arising from stimulation of the genitals, do they not belong to you either?<br /> <br /> Or is the issue that there's a separation between the Exaltation and the homunculus inside of a person's head?<br /> <br /> Are Inspire actions also objectionable for creating emotions from the external side of the dichotomy between false outer influences and genuine inner influences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm... this is off topic, but I'll indulge. Keep in mind, this is all my opinion, not backed up by any edition's firm canon on the subject, and is purely how I view/play it.<br /> <br /> Exaltation changes what you are. It's not a seperate force, not a magical power battery spot welded to your soul. Your powers are your own, formed from your abilities and skills. You're uplifted, and while there's still a human at your core, behind the wheel, you are different afterwards than before. Hence Second Breath. You aren't a person with an Exaltation, you are Exalted. That doesn't mean 'you're not human', but it means that the abilities and skill of a Chosen are very firmly inherent. Whatever you feel in that moment of change is your reaction to it.<br /> <br /> Essence Fever, as I read it, doesn't <i>contradict</i> that idea but undercuts it. The Essence is inside you! It wants to be used! It's making you feel excited. It's playing Exaltation more as a power up, an External source you draw upon, which is not against the text of the setting (and is <i>way </i>closer to how it all works mechanically), but is very much not what I prefer. Same with the Incarne explicitly choosing their Exalts, and the idea of theming Abyssal charms more around the Deathlords. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good. We've got so many interesting characters and scenarios because that notion that they've got to have an enormous scope of perspective in the long term has been dropped. </div> </div> </div>Mmm. I'm gonna try Alucard's thing. Isator, mind letting up on this point? I disagree, <i>hard</i>, but we don't need an edition war every five bloody seconds. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think one could plausibly make a game in which an Integrity focused Zenith who continues to view themselves as a humble monk is continuously challenged by beings looking to tempt them, or political figures trying to convince them towards grandeur, power and direct authority or continuously resisted by somebody trying to maintain perspective, humility and simple good works. People witness that, hear of it, and find hope in the idea, wanting to follow the example set.<br /> <br /> It's one way for the world to become better. </div> </div> </div>This gets into wider questions of personal morality though. Is it moral for an Exalt to choose non action? To limit themselves and what they do to the most humble personal level?<br /> <br /> I guess 'moral ambiguity is good' but I don't see an 'act like you would as a mortal' take as... anything appropriate for an Exalt. It's abdication of responsibility in a world as messed up as Creation. Someone without the will to act just doesn't seem like a good candidate for Exaltation to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T19:26:32-07:00","id":1324600,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue I\u2019m running into is getting a little too caught up in my character\u2019s personal struggles, because sometimes they mirror my own. <br /> <br /> She is struggling with moving on from her home, because when she left it to join the game, she was doing so with the motivation of \u2018become stronger to better-protect by home.\u2019<br /> <br /> This is not dissimilar to my own desire to better myself so I can better provide for my home and family, \u2018protecting\u2019 them from the problems of the world.<br /> <br /> She has trouble recognizing her value as an Exalt because she fears becoming something other than herself (I wrote that with a mind on what a former Immaculate would think, becoming an \u2018Anathema\u2019.\u2019<br /> <br /> This mirrors my struggles with my own self-worth, wherein gaining the confidence to act really does feel like a newly-found super power.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the issue of being able to leave home and know that things will be okay...well the last time that happened, a Gold-Faction-Influenced Zenith monk showed up, moved into her old home and started a Realm-hating Solar-worshipping cult, and now there\u2019s an army coming to get them. So yeah, she\u2019s not really feeling the idea that she can just leave home for an extended period and everything will be okay.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a parallel for that, just...talk about responsibility!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T03:21:07-07:00","id":1324680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324445#post1324445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Essence is inside you! It wants to be used! It's making you feel excited. It's playing Exaltation more as a power up, an External source you draw upon, which is not against the text of the setting (and is <i>way </i>closer to how it all works mechanically), but is very much not what I prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you're saying about Essence is identical to how hormones work. Are hormones something external?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess 'moral ambiguity is good' but I don't see an 'act like you would as a mortal' take as... anything appropriate for an Exalt. It's abdication of responsibility in a world as messed up as Creation. Someone without the will to act just doesn't seem like a good candidate for Exaltation to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Integrity-focused Zenith uses the Integrity Charms.<br /> <br /> This isn't about limiting oneself to mortal action, it's about being principled and incorruptible in the manner of Jesus or Siddhartha Gautama. Principled in a manner that keeps you on course and is an inspiration to others.<br /> <br /> If that's not a valid expression for Solar Exalted, what would the point of Supernal Integrity be?<br /> <br /> A person isn't limited to mortal activity because they're not drafting plans for world domination, grand mystical artifice, or statues of themselves. An Exalt in the role of sage or prophet who maintains that they're nothing special is not technically accurate (unless it's less about measuring capability and more about assessment of character and moral fortitude, and how they should be treated by others), but it's a fine and compelling standard for a person to set and adhere to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T03:25:15-07:00","id":1324681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324600#post1324600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue I\u2019m running into is getting a little too caught up in my character\u2019s personal struggles, because sometimes they mirror my own. <br /> <br /> She is struggling with moving on from her home, because when she left it to join the game, she was doing so with the motivation of \u2018become stronger to better-protect by home.\u2019<br /> <br /> This is not dissimilar to my own desire to better myself so I can better provide for my home and family, \u2018protecting\u2019 them from the problems of the world.<br /> <br /> She has trouble recognizing her value as an Exalt because she fears becoming something other than herself (I wrote that with a mind on what a former Immaculate would think, becoming an \u2018Anathema\u2019.\u2019<br /> <br /> This mirrors my struggles with my own self-worth, wherein gaining the confidence to act really does feel like a newly-found super power.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the issue of being able to leave home and know that things will be okay...well the last time that happened, a Gold-Faction-Influenced Zenith monk showed up, moved into her old home and started a Realm-hating Solar-worshipping cult, and now there\u2019s an army coming to get them. So yeah, she\u2019s not really feeling the idea that she can just leave home for an extended period and everything will be okay.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a parallel for that, just...talk about responsibility!</div> </div> </div> </div>So is this a matter of feeling like you're projecting yourself into the character in ways that you don't actually want the fiction to go in the direction of, or are fine with the characterisation but it's just uncomfortably too real sometimes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T03:53:25-07:00","id":1324686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324680#post1324680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything you're saying about Essence is identical to how hormones work. Are hormones something external?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this context, yeah? Of course they're <i>physically </i>internal but they're something that affects you, your mental state and the choices you make. You would make different choices if they weren't active, so those feelings are not entirely 'of you'. They're an external factor even if not physically external. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Integrity-focused Zenith uses the Integrity Charms.<br /> <br /> This isn't about limiting oneself to mortal action, it's about being principled and incorruptible in the manner of Jesus or Siddhartha Gautama. Principled in a manner that keeps you on course and is an inspiration to others.<br /> <br /> If that's not a valid expression for Solar Exalted, what would the point of Supernal Integrity be? </div> </div> </div>Supernal was only added this edition. It could be 'treating all 25 Abilities equally' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A person isn't limited to mortal activity because they're not drafting plans for world domination, grand mystical artifice, or statues of themselves. An Exalt in the role of sage or prophet who maintains that they're nothing special is not technically accurate (unless it's less about measuring capability and more about assessment of character and moral fortitude, and how they should be treated by others), but it's a fine and compelling standard for a person to set and adhere to. </div> </div> </div>But the topic here is a character who <i>does </i>want to be limited. Who wants to be a simple humble monk from a simple humble valley and is uncomfortable with the sage/prophet role. Even if they don't wear crowns and don't conquer the world, you're still describing a traditional Exalted type of character. (Your examples were two of the world's most famous religious figures). Not everyone wants that path","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T04:04:13-07:00","id":1324687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324600#post1324600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue I\u2019m running into is getting a little too caught up in my character\u2019s personal struggles, because sometimes they mirror my own.<br /> <br /> She is struggling with moving on from her home, because when she left it to join the game, she was doing so with the motivation of \u2018become stronger to better-protect by home.\u2019<br /> <br /> This is not dissimilar to my own desire to better myself so I can better provide for my home and family, \u2018protecting\u2019 them from the problems of the world.<br /> <br /> She has trouble recognizing her value as an Exalt because she fears becoming something other than herself (I wrote that with a mind on what a former Immaculate would think, becoming an \u2018Anathema\u2019.\u2019<br /> <br /> This mirrors my struggles with my own self-worth, wherein gaining the confidence to act really does feel like a newly-found super power.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the issue of being able to leave home and know that things will be okay...well the last time that happened, a Gold-Faction-Influenced Zenith monk showed up, moved into her old home and started a Realm-hating Solar-worshipping cult, and now there\u2019s an army coming to get them. So yeah, she\u2019s not really feeling the idea that she can just leave home for an extended period and everything will be okay.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a parallel for that, just...talk about responsibility!</div> </div> </div> </div>(See, this is why most of my characters get kicked out of their homeland in their background. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Makes it easy!)<br /> <br /> Some decisions really don't have easy answers. We as people want a 'right answer' to set things together properly and just move on, but not every situation provides that. The only advice I can give metatextually is that if a situation seems to have no right answers, it's the job of an Exalt to forge one.<br /> <br /> Ex3 opens with two quotes. One from Tanith Lee that... I still don't understand why they put there. But the far, far better one, and my pick for best part of the entire core book, is this line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nearly all men can withstand adversity, but if you want to test a man\u2019s character, give him power. </div> </div> </div>It will forever be the game's core conflict. You have the power to resolve your situations in Exalted, all you need is to think of how, what consequences you can accept and which you can't. You could train your own monks to keep the valley safe while you're gone, throw the local Realm outpost into chaos so they can't focus on your home, sett the Gold Factionate to rights by arguing philosophy with him and guiding him down a more peaceful path. All these things are doable, and they don't make you a different person. It's just realizing what you can do..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T04:26:08-07:00","id":1324689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324600#post1324600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She has trouble recognizing her value as an Exalt because she fears becoming something other than herself (I wrote that with a mind on what a former Immaculate would think, becoming an \u2018Anathema\u2019.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>Well something to remember, the Immaculate Order teaches that the Anathema are essentially demons. So while your character has a lifetime of teachings telling her that she is a demon, she has the experience of exalting. Of feeling holy, of feeling endowed with a power that does not feel demonic in the slightest. <br /> <br /> She would know instinctively that she is not a demon. There is no hidden voice encouraging her to commit atrocities (Not unless she gains Whispers). Yes, she doesn't know what she is, or what it even means to be a solar. She will need to reconcile the immaculate beliefs with who she is, or flat out reject them. Maybe she views the teachings as something that should be a metaphor for power instead of literally being a demon. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T05:52:52-07:00","id":1324706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324686#post1324686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this context, yeah? Of course they're <i>physically </i>internal but they're something that affects you, your mental state and the choices you make. You would make different choices if they weren't active, so those feelings are not entirely 'of you'. They're an external factor even if not physically external.</div> </div> </div> </div>No human being in existence has ever functioned in the manner to which you're referring. The choices you would make in the absence of conditioned habits and biochemical pathway impulses are so far removed from what you actually are that it could not even meaningfully be described as you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal was only added this edition. It could be 'treating all 25 Abilities equally' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They're not equal. Even in the absence of Supernal, they all have different applicability and different levels of narrative buy-in. Some are even versatile enough that they can demand a lot more buy-in when focused on; combat Abilities come out about the same no matter what kinds of stories they end up in, whereas Socialize is something that can range from a tertiary Ability employed in a utilitarian fashion for the occasional social influence action where it fits more than Presence or Performance, to games heavily focused on courtly intrigue, community organisation and agitation, and societal engineering, and with the benefit of Charms all the way into narratives constructing a variety of identities to engage in a number of different contexts.<br /> <br /> Integrity is closer to the latter. The value of Supernal is that it allows one to designate a characteristic Ability in which one doesn't hit a ceiling early and become obligated to develop laterally, allowing for it to be a much heavier focus for a character.<br /> <br /> And it's a more internal and somewhat reactive Ability, so in a scenario such as this it could reconcile elements by allowing a character to be an example of Solar heroism by means of the way that things are resisted and one's core identity is preserved. It's a thing with literary and mythic precedent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants to be a simple humble monk from a simple humble valley and is uncomfortable with the sage/prophet role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that raises the question of exactly what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24172_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24172\" data-vbnamecard=\"24172\">Sticks</a> envisions the role and activity of even the simple monk to be. I would need more precision to be able to say anything I would be more sure might be helpful.<br /> <br /> I do wonder somewhat if part of the issue is that Sticks is working off of an assumption of what it means for a character to &quot;graduate&quot; to a &quot;proper&quot; Exalted level which is not necessarily accurate; if it pertains to doing or being something that has always been very popular in exaggerated Internet discussions but is ultimately a very narrow slice of what works with the mechanics, game influences, and general variety in humanity, society and emotional outlooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone wants that path</div> </div> </div> </div>My previous statement being said, you're correct of course; even I was focused too much on a sense of grand scope that the game is not pushing so heavily anymore. The setting is already displaying greater awareness of its own scope being larger than any of the Exalted, so ultimately there really is nothing preventing somebody's life (within the scope of a played game, if perhaps not the full scale of an Exalted lifespan) from being focused down to something the size of a valley.<br /> <br /> Certainly, we have several Lunar Dominions depicting narratives of that form, including another who is a monk. Did you get a look at those yourself, Sticks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T06:34:33-07:00","id":1324715,"title":"","content":"Before enlightenment, chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment, chop wood, carry water.<br /> <br /> (Or at least, in the case of the Knight Raiton, &quot;solve murders, punch murderers.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T06:56:23-07:00","id":1324724,"title":"","content":"All my simple monk wants to do is hang out with his brothers, tend vegetables, do morning and evening prayers, sacrifice captives to satiate the elder gods dreaming in the Void, copy texts, do some light reading, meditate, etc.<br /> <br /> Normal simple monk stuff.<br /> <br /> But unfortunately his monastery's been stolen, his brothers turned into mad cannibals, and the ancient horror trapped beneath the monastery is now free (and... dealing drugs?).<br /> So he has to go stop it.<br /> <br /> But he doesn't go on about how he's a Solar, saviour of the world, etc, etc, because he still just thinks of himself as a normal monk.<br /> He really just wants to go back to his normal life. He'd rather not be trying to save the land, he'd rather go to the library and read. But you've got to do what you've got to do.<br /> <br /> I suppose the issue is that if we do succeed in saving the day, putting his monastery back where it should be, destroying or trapping the High Priest Not to Be Described (aka the Elder Heirophant, aka the Tcho-tcho Lama of Leng), then this character has no motivation to continue adventuring. He will, after all, just want to go back to being a high priest.<br /> <br /> This is fine by me, because I'll just bring back my old Lunar character.<br /> <br /> But a lot of people wouldn't want to do this. The issue with a reluctant hero is it's fine as long as there's stuff pulling them back into heroism (which means they can't be too reluctant).<br /> <br /> But then, Alazar has no-one telling him he's an amazing prophet-hero. I guess the question is how well the character resists the blandishments of flatterers and stays true to their vows/realises they have a responsibility to the world and must sacrifice their simple life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T07:44:28-07:00","id":1324733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324724#post1324724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the issue is that if we do succeed in saving the day, putting his monastery back where it should be, destroying or trapping the High Priest Not to Be Described (aka the Elder Heirophant, aka the Tcho-tcho Lama of Leng), then this character has no motivation to continue adventuring. He will, after all, just want to go back to being a high priest.<br /> <br /> This is fine by me, because I'll just bring back my old Lunar character.<br /> <br /> But a lot of people wouldn't want to do this. The issue with a reluctant hero is it's fine as long as there's stuff pulling them back into heroism (which means they can't be too reluctant).<br /> <br /> But then, Alazar has no-one telling him he's an amazing prophet-hero. I guess the question is how well the character resists the blandishments of flatterers and stays true to their vows/realises they have a responsibility to the world and must sacrifice their simple life.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people don't want their character to just retire, sounds like it is conversation with the ST to create a hook or story to keep their character out of retirement. Something to motivate them where going out will further protect the monastery than staying around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T11:47:35-07:00","id":1324782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324312#post1324312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Introduced is introduced. Moreover, Holden said otherwise; I'm having trouble finding the post, but he actually discussed at one point how he himself assumed it was an editing error, until he talked to Grabowski during the development of Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still setting aside how it was presented as doing what Limit does now. The vague concept might have been introduced, but judging by the text of 1e and 3e, 3e's Essence fever is different under the hood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T14:38:21-07:00","id":1324817,"title":"","content":"It\u00b4s nice to hear that after I started my Hormone Replacement Therapy and started an intake of foreign hormones, I stopped being me, and neither my actions or my feelings were mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Very very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T16:12:26-07:00","id":1324828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324817#post1324817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u00b4s nice to hear that after I started my Hormone Replacement Therapy and started an intake of foreign hormones, I stopped being me, and neither my actions or my feelings were mine.<br /> <br /> Very very nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I meant. My whole point was that hormones are irrelevant to who you are. They're a physical factor to be dealt with that can affect your thoughts and actions but who you are goes beyond that IMO <br /> <br /> I guess that's the debate. I say Exaltation is something inherent to you that transcends other factors, while I feel the current canon leans more towards portraying Exaltation as external, through the essence fever thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T16:52:40-07:00","id":1324831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324828#post1324828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not what I meant. My whole point was that hormones are irrelevant to who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're irrelevant, then why did Clophiroth have to get them replaced? If who I am is irrespective of the chemicals my brain produces, then how is it that so many people who suffer head injuries come away from it changed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324828#post1324828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're a physical factor to be dealt with that can affect your thoughts and actions but who you are goes beyond that IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can believe in souls and whatnot, but so far no one's been able to prove that you aren't made up of the things that make up your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-15-2019, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T23:01:46-07:00","id":1324893,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, you\u2019re citing an example of proving a negative to justify continuing to argue with Croakamancer. It\u2019s not helpful and it just makes you seem like somebody who looks to pick arguments.<br /> <br /> The real issue for my monk comes down to responsibility. Is her greater responsibility to her valley and the people and spirits who live there, or is it to Creation and it\u2019s problems?<br /> <br /> Her sifu (not WiFi) told her to go out and don\u2019t come back until there are epic poems about her to share. Her party does have a responsibility to stop this rogue Sidereal and save Creation, and she has an outstanding promise to fulfill towards her Abyssal girlfriend. She\u2019s going to leave the valley, but how can she do so with a clear conscience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T00:52:01-07:00","id":1324908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324893#post1324893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real issue for my monk comes down to responsibility. Is her greater responsibility to her valley and the people and spirits who live there, or is it to Creation and it\u2019s problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that\u2019s up to you, isn\u2019t it? <br /> <br /> On the one hand, your valley and the spirits are <i>part</i> of Creation. It could very well be argued that changing the world starts at home. <br /> <br /> But on the other hand, if this single Sidereal is literally a threat to the continued existence of the entire world, then letting them succeed would by definition be a threat to the continued existence of your home as well.<br /> <br /> But back on the first hand, do you think this is a problem you can meaningfully help solve? Because if you feel that it\u2019s beyond you, there\u2019s lots of heroes in Creation.<br /> <br /> But then again, \u201cthe scales might be tipped by a single grain of rice\u201d and all that. <br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014<br /> <br /> One time I was playing a Dawn Caste brawler; his buddy, an Eclipse, had been spirited away to the Demon City (or so we believed) by two Green Sun Princes. My character really wanted to help, but didn\u2019t know the first thing about demons or the Demon City, so he attended a fighting tournament instead of going after them. <br /> <br /> He figured since the tournament was sponsored by a high-profile god, he could get an audience with the god if he won the tournament and see if the god had anything he could lend my brawler to help with his Eclipse situation. <br /> <br /> (It was rumored the god had a magic key that could take the user instantly into the Demon City, but when I won, he ended up giving me armor and bracers and told my my strength of arm was all I needed.)<br /> <br /> Of course, once we found out that the Eclipse was still being held in <i>Creation</i>, we hauled ass after him, had a climactic battle with the Infernals, and our own Zenith put his daiklave through the Eclipse for reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T02:34:21-07:00","id":1324916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324831#post1324831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're irrelevant, then why did Clophiroth have to get them replaced? If who I am is irrespective of the chemicals my brain produces, then how is it that so many people who suffer head injuries come away from it changed?<br /> <br /> Sure, you can believe in souls and whatnot, but so far no one's been able to prove that you aren't made up of the things that make up your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Sticks said, this is an effectively endless argument, since it's a contest between strict physicality and things which can not be proven. However, in a fantasy setting such as Exalted, <i>where souls literally and provably exist,</i> I don't think my take of wanting Exaltation to be more spiritual enlightenment than external power up is a bad one? 'We're more than the sum of our parts' really shouldn't be that out there a belief, it doesn't even really imply any kind of strong religious belief, does it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T02:41:30-07:00","id":1324918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324893#post1324893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, you\u2019re citing an example of proving a negative to justify continuing to argue with Croakamancer. It\u2019s not helpful and it just makes you seem like somebody who looks to pick arguments.<br /> <br /> The real issue for my monk comes down to responsibility. Is her greater responsibility to her valley and the people and spirits who live there, or is it to Creation and it\u2019s problems?<br /> <br /> Her sifu (not WiFi) told her to go out and don\u2019t come back until there are epic poems about her to share. Her party does have a responsibility to stop this rogue Sidereal and save Creation, and she has an outstanding promise to fulfill towards her Abyssal girlfriend. She\u2019s going to leave the valley, but how can she do so with a clear conscience?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarify all you want Sticks, you won't convince me Lou-Khan isn't secretly the world's first and deadliest LOLCat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly, the answer to your question is simply 'have a plan'. You want a path forward with a clear conscience, that's fine, you just need to do... something. There's a bunch of potential resolutions to this situation. Start giving the valley some teachings of your own, leave Wind there to watch over it (after giving him a good talking to and setting him straight), get A Very Handsome And Dashing Sorcerer to try and use a Working to make the Valley harder to access from the outside.. So long as you make an effort to come up with <i>some </i>kind of long term plan to keep the valley safe, leaving with a clear conscience is fairly reasonable.<br /> <br /> You just need the will to act. The will to accept that things may have to change a little to keep people safe.That takes a little effort IC, but it's good character conflict IMO. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T03:29:09-07:00","id":1324923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324916#post1324916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Sticks said, this is an effectively endless argument, since it's a contest between strict physicality and things which can not be proven. However, in a fantasy setting such as Exalted, <i>where souls literally and provably exist,</i> I don't think my take of wanting Exaltation to be more spiritual enlightenment than external power up is a bad one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a reminder, if a person soul literally, provably exists in the Exalted setting, then it\u2019s part of that person, just as your real-world brain chemicals are part of you.<br /> <br /> If your Essence is telling you to go out and do stuff, that\u2019s from you. It\u2019s <i>your</i> Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T03:51:03-07:00","id":1324927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324916#post1324916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, in a fantasy setting such as Exalted, <i>where souls literally and provably exist,</i> I don't think my take of wanting Exaltation to be more spiritual enlightenment than external power up is a bad one?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not bad, but it's never been how the game presented Exaltation, so it's not really something to get hung up on.<br /> <br /> Especially when advising another person who doesn't share those priorities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'We're more than the sum of our parts' really shouldn't be that out there a belief, it doesn't even really imply any kind of strong religious belief, does it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, but it does imply that recognising that the parts still exist.<br /> <br /> A person is more than the sum of their parts, and yet will still die very quickly if their heart stops pumping, or a clot blocks blood flow to many parts of their brain. Virtually every part of you is intertwined and interdependent, there's no aspect that can be isolated and declared non Grata without consequence.<br /> <br /> The statement that one's chemical makeup and pathways are irrelevant to one's core identity do not validate the self, they perpetuate ignorance about it by refusal to perceive all of its influences. If there's anything transcendent about a person (and I believe there is) it's evidently not something that can remotely dictate action devoid of mood or habit or other things found in neural pathways.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Essence Fever is not operating in a setting that acts as though there is a dichotomy between body and soul; souls exist, but Gnostic contempt for the flesh does not. There's a good deal more of things deriving from some Asian spiritual systems, in which material and immaterial are intertwined and interdependent.<br /> <br /> Hence Exalted power manifesting through Abilities and Attributes. Exaltation is not going to be purely transcendent when it needs to flow through the limbs and the breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324893#post1324893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is her greater responsibility to her valley and the people and spirits who live there, or is it to Creation and it\u2019s problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation and its problems are so big, a single person might crack under the strain of them. There's a reason that there was a Deliberative. In the absence of one, a person can't fairly have it held against them to prioritize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She\u2019s going to leave the valley, but how can she do so with a clear conscience?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like she can't. That seems to me to be something to lean into as a source of character conflict; being troubled and dissatisfied for having left something behind.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the intention is to not be that anymore, development towards that seems simple; if the character is driven by compassion, then her compassion was less driven by things distant and abstract than it is by people who are right in front of her. This is arguably less about the scope of Exalted then it is about somebody who would already want to do good, and just needs a push out of her comfort zone to get the ball rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T06:17:13-07:00","id":1324950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324893#post1324893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;177&quot;]<br /> The real issue for my monk comes down to responsibility. Is her greater responsibility to her valley and the people and spirits who live there, or is it to Creation and it\u2019s problems?<br /> <br /> Her sifu (not WiFi) told her to go out and don\u2019t come back until there are epic poems about her to share. Her party does have a responsibility to stop this rogue Sidereal and save Creation, and she has an outstanding promise to fulfill towards her Abyssal girlfriend. She\u2019s going to leave the valley, but how can she do so with a clear conscience?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sifu is literally telling her to leave. Meaning that the Sifu believes that the valley will be OK in the meantime. <br /> <br /> Now of course it is ok to have some hand wringing as your character leaves, and some trepidation that all will be OK while you're away from the valley. But at the same time, there's tremendous responsibility to stop the rogue Siddy. <br /> <br /> Chalk it up to, &quot;I'd rather not leave, but I will return as soon as possible.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T09:10:07-07:00","id":1324979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324950#post1324950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sifu is literally telling her to leave. Meaning that the Sifu believes that the valley will be OK in the meantime. </div> </div> </div> </div>It can also be read as a character who cares less about that homeland. Certainly, I would find the demand in terms of getting epic poems to be a red flag.<br /> <br /> But I couldn't say what the sifu's player intends for the character's motives and priorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T09:28:45-07:00","id":1324981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324121-to-be-a-hero-or-to-be-human?p=1324979#post1324979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can also be read as a character who cares less about that homeland. Certainly, I would find the demand in terms of getting epic poems to be a red flag.<br /> <br /> But I couldn't say what the sifu's player intends for the character's motives and priorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Sifu wants the monk to use her powers for good, and to carry out widespread assistance and help, so tried to send her off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}